WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:15.539
Because of the lagoon adventure, the Indians became Peter's friends.

2
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.381
Peter had saved Tiger Lily's life.

3
00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:24.204
Now she and her tribe kept faithful watch over the Lost Boys' underground home.

4
00:00:25.664 --> 00:00:28.066
Night and day, they guarded Peter and his family.

5
00:00:29.386 --> 00:00:33.837
They called Peter "The Great White Father," which he quite liked.

6
00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:41.362
He would say to them, "The Great White Father is glad to see the warriors protecting his home

7
00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:42.383
from the pirates."

8
00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:46.946
But Tiger Lily did not want Wendy to be called Peter's wife.

9
00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:51.529
The Indian princess had become quite fond of the little boy as well.

10
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.952
And, like Tinker Bell, she was jealous of Wendy.

11
00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:03.317
One evening, the Indians were at their watch as usual while the children were having dinner below.

12
00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.278
Peter wasn't home because he had gone to find out the time.

13
00:01:08.418 --> 00:01:11.999
On the island, one found out the time by finding the crocodile.

14
00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:17.781
When the clock inside the crocodile struck the hour, one knew what time it was.

15
00:01:19.341 --> 00:01:23.762
The meal was make-believe, and the boys were particularly noisy and difficult.

16
00:01:24.782 --> 00:01:26.123
Wendy asked for silence.

17
00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:32.933
"If you have any complaints," she said, "you must first raise your hands to speak."

18
00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.854
All their hands went up at once.

19
00:01:35.874 --> 00:01:39.716
"Slightly is eating all the food!"

20
00:01:39.736 --> 00:01:42.217
"Nibs is sneezing on the table!"

21
00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:45.379
"The twins took too much dessert!"

22
00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:48.420
"Curly isn't using his knife and fork!"

23
00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:52.662
After the meal, things quieted down.

24
00:01:53.823 --> 00:01:56.564
They all helped clean the table and put the door away.

25
00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:01.381
Wendy went back to her sewing while the boys danced and played by the fire.

26
00:02:02.561 --> 00:02:06.423
It was a familiar scene in their home, perhaps for the last time.

27
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:10.704
Suddenly they could hear footsteps above them.

28
00:02:10.724 --> 00:02:15.345
"Children, that must be your father," said Wendy.

29
00:02:15.365 --> 00:02:18.066
"He likes it when you greet him."

30
00:02:19.446 --> 00:02:22.287
Outside, Peter was saying good night to the Indians.

31
00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:25.448
"Keep a safe watch over us tonight!"

32
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.142
he said, before slipping into his tree.

33
00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:35.487
When he opened the round door underground, the children joyfully dragged him from his tunnel.

34
00:02:36.607 --> 00:02:40.150
Peter had brought nuts for the boys and the time of day for Wendy.

35
00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:44.833
"Peter, you will spoil them, you know," Wendy said.

36
00:02:44.853 --> 00:02:51.818
"Father," said Curly, "we're dancing and we want you to dance with us."

37
00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:58.141
Peter liked dancing, but for fun he pretended to be a tired father coming home from work.

38
00:02:58.161 --> 00:03:01.083
"Me?" he groaned.

39
00:03:01.103 --> 00:03:04.184
"My old bones can hardly walk!"

40
00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:09.326
"And we want Mother to dance too," said Slightly.

41
00:03:09.346 --> 00:03:13.448
"What?" cried Wendy, joining the game.

42
00:03:13.468 --> 00:03:18.110
"This old mother of so many boys has lots to do!"

43
00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.751
"But it's Saturday night!"

44
00:03:22.412 --> 00:03:23.152
shouted Michael.

45
00:03:24.192 --> 00:03:27.635
However, no one knew if it was really Saturday night.

46
00:03:29.016 --> 00:03:31.718
They had lost count of the days of the week long ago.

47
00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:38.564
When they wanted to have a special evening, they always called it "Saturday night."

48
00:03:41.647 --> 00:03:46.471
Peter and Wendy promised to dance with them, but first the boys would have to put on their

49
00:03:46.511 --> 00:03:48.072
pajamas and get ready for bed.

50
00:03:49.373 --> 00:03:52.796
While they waited for the boys, Peter joined Wendy at the fire.

51
00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.221
She looked at him lovingly.

52
00:03:55.241 --> 00:03:59.663
"They are sweet, our little family, don't you think?"

53
00:04:00.404 --> 00:04:01.044
said Wendy.

54
00:04:02.165 --> 00:04:03.525
Peter suddenly looked troubled.

55
00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:05.126
"What is it, Peter?"

56
00:04:05.146 --> 00:04:10.309
"It's only make-believe that I am their father, right?"

57
00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:13.050
replied Peter in a shaky voice.

58
00:04:14.871 --> 00:04:16.752
"Oh, yes," said Wendy.

59
00:04:16.772 --> 00:04:23.076
"You see," he continued, "it would make me old to be their real father."

60
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.722
"Peter, after all this time together, what do I mean to you?"

61
00:04:29.542 --> 00:04:30.182
asked Wendy.

62
00:04:31.983 --> 00:04:34.064
His answer was not what she had hoped for.

63
00:04:34.084 --> 00:04:38.446
"I am your devoted son," replied Peter.

64
00:04:38.466 --> 00:04:44.989
"I understand," she said, but it really was very confusing.

65
00:04:46.409 --> 00:04:49.570
Wendy got up from her seat and went to another corner of the room.

66
00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:54.474
"Sometimes you are very strange," Peter said to her.

67
00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.958
"And so is Tiger Lily.

68
00:04:57.979 --> 00:05:01.966
She says she wants to mean something to me, but doesn't want to be my mother."

69
00:05:01.986 --> 00:05:07.795
"Perhaps Tinker Bell can explain it to you," Wendy answered, frowning.
